i/articleshow/135558335.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135558335.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/respect-seniors-end-bjp-rss-hatred-rijijus-seven-point-advice-to-rahul-gandhi/articleshow/135558335.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/respect-seniors-end-bjp-rss-hatred-rijijus-seven-point-advice-to-rahul-gandhi/articleshow/135558335.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-05T09:41:41+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Aadrita Halder</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135558529,imgsize-1059552.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Centre proposes immediate suspension of licences for substandard drugs]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/centre-proposes-immediate-suspension-of-licences-for-substandard-drugs/articleshow/135557911.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135557911.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[The Health Ministry has introduced new regulations aimed at suspending manufacturing licenses for medicines that do not meet quality criteria. This swift action is intended to stop subpar drugs from reaching patients and to minimize their circulation during the regulatory review. Licenses can be suspended based on government analysts' findings that indicate deficiencies.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/centre-proposes-immediate-suspension-of-licences-for-substandard-drugs/articleshow/135557911.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/centre-proposes-immediate-suspension-of-licences-for-substandard-drugs/articleshow/135557911.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-05T09:31:19+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Anuja Jaiswal</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135558170,imgsize-83208.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Changing NEET-PG to rank-based system won’t fix structural problems, doctors say]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/changing-neet-pg-to-rank-based-system-wont-fix-structural-problems-doctors-say/articleshow/135557710.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135557710.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Altering the merit-list approach for NEET-PG and NEET-SS without resolving core structural issues proves to be insufficient. In a recent meeting, stakeholders voiced concerns regarding excessive fees, low stipends, and compulsory bonds. The government primarily pointed to state authority on these matters, indicating a need for greater regulation. Attendees advocated for improved faculty hiring, fair stipends, and independent audits to enhance the quality of medical education.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/changing-neet-pg-to-rank-based-system-wont-fix-structural-problems-doctors-say/articleshow/135557710.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/changing-neet-pg-to-rank-based-system-wont-fix-structural-problems-doctors-say/articleshow/135557710.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-05T09:18:09+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Anuja Jaiswal</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135557835,imgsize-61429.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Noida airport among 10 new gateways proposed for drug imports]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/noida-airport-among-10-new-gateways-proposed-for-drug-imports/articleshow/135557390.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace